Make symmetrize_sparsity deterministic. The threads append the entries
that pad the sparsity pattern in the order they reach the critical
section, so the graph given to METIS/Scotch, and with it the fill-reducing
ordering, changes from run to run with OMP_NUM_THREADS > 1. Sort the
padded entries of each row (all zeros), which gives the same graph as a
single thread. Fixes the random failures of SPARSE_seq_27 and
SPARSE_seq_77 (cavity16, 8 threads).

diff --git a/src/sparse/CompressedSparseMatrix.cpp b/src/sparse/CompressedSparseMatrix.cpp
index 5140374b..73be1429 100644
--- a/src/sparse/CompressedSparseMatrix.cpp
+++ b/src/sparse/CompressedSparseMatrix.cpp
@@ -184,6 +184,13 @@ namespace strumpack {
             }
           }
         }
+      // the threads above append the padded entries in a
+      // nondeterministic order, sort them to get the same graph (and
+      // reordering) as with a single thread
+#pragma omp parallel for
+      for (integer_t i=0; i<n_; i++)
+        std::sort(a2_ind.begin()+a2_ptr[i]+(ptr_[i+1]-ptr_[i]),
+                  a2_ind.begin()+a2_ptr[i+1]);
       std::swap(ptr_, a2_ptr);
       std::swap(ind_, a2_ind);
       std::swap(val_, a2_val);
